# Repository Workflow

Prefer a consistent Makefile interface across projects:

```text
make tools
make generate
make manifests
make fmt
make vet
make lint
make test
make test-envtest
make test-e2e
make test-reconcile
make docker-build
make helm-lint
make security
make verify
```

Not every repository needs every target on day one, but equivalent actions should use equivalent names.

PRs should keep generated files in sync and should not mix unrelated architectural changes.

Use RFC/ADR review for:
- public API changes;
- API-group/domain decisions;
- security-boundary changes;
- new cross-project conventions;
- generator architecture;
- destructive cloud lifecycle semantics.

Use reusable GitHub Actions where possible rather than copy-pasting workflow logic across repositories.
